  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CPO 801 addresses on strengthening employer engagement in shaping inclusive and sustainable labour market policies in Cambodia, especially within the context of the Global Accelerator on Jobs and Social Protection for Just Transitions (GA). As a newly designated GA pathfinder country, Cambodia is committed to developing a roadmap supporting decent job creation, social protection, and structural transformations, including green and digital transitions. The CPO aims to enhance the capacity of employers&apos; organizations to contribute effectively to this process, ensuring their input informs evidence-based policy dialogue and national strategies for sustainable enterprise development.  During the biennium, the expected results include the active participation of employer organizations in the design and implementation of the GA roadmap, as well as strengthened capacity to advocate for job-rich, inclusive reforms. Employer organizations will also improve their ability to generate research and analysis to inform policy decisions. This involves building their capacity to assess labour market trends, skills gaps, and social protection systems, while effectively communicating their positions. Through targeted training and research activities, employer representatives will gain a deeper understanding of labour law, social dialogue, and conflict resolution, fostering a more cooperative industrial relations environment. The primary beneficiaries are employers&apos; organizations and their members, particularly those looking to contribute to national development strategies. Indirectly, workers and enterprises will benefit from improved dialogue and advocacy that promote decent work and sustainable economic growth. The strategy is implemented in coordination with national stakeholders and international development partners, aligning Cambodia&#x2019;s policy approaches with global goals of just transition and inclusive development.</narrative>
  </description>
